<section class="section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="split">
    <div class="intro">
      <div class="eyebrow">FAQ</div>
      <h2 id="faq-title">Fair questions.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details open>
        <summary>Is the value a real offer?</summary>
        <p>No. It's an estimate built from reference scrap prices per kilo and a visual weight estimate. Actual offers depend on purity, volume and your region — Wastetide can get you those.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How accurate is the weight?</summary>
        <p>It's read from the photo, so it's approximate. Shoot the whole pile in daylight and include something of known size (a pallet, a door, a person) to tighten the estimate. Each material shows how confident the model is.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What happens to my photo?</summary>
        <p>It's uploaded to run the analysis and attached to your result. Don't include people's faces or documents you wouldn't want stored.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What happens after 3 free scans?</summary>
        <p>Leave your work email to unlock 10 more. If you need to scan every shipment, Wastetide does it continuously and finds buyers for you.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I scan hazardous waste?</summary>
        <p>WasteScope recognises batteries and circuit boards, but it doesn't classify hazardous waste or fill regulatory forms. For that, use Wastetide's BSD (France) and e-Manifest (US) tools.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

